  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed value near $13.02B (-0.3% 30D) leaves tokenized-cash balances largely range-bound\u2014the market story this week is more about issuer and distribution news than a shift in AUM. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/tempo-earn-embedded-stablecoin-yield-deel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tempo Launches Embedded Yield Product for Platforms, Starting With Deel</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~40% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~38% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~8% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/01/citi-goldman-other-global-banks-and-asset-managers-team-up-on-stablecoin-venture\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Citi, Goldman, other global banks and asset managers team up on stablecoin venture</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Multi-chain footprints are a distribution signal:</strong> Funds listing many networks with thin holder counts usually signal jurisdictional or distribution reach, not deep secondary liquidity on every chain. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/01/ethena-pushes-stablecoins-into-everyday-banking-with-high-yield-savings-cards-and-payments\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ethena pushes stablecoins into everyday banking with high-yield savings, cards and payments</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Rates still matter as much as product and chain choice:</strong> Rate and money-market moves can reshape fund-level inflows as quickly as any chain or product launch story. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/09/01/bitcoin-consolidates-near-usd78-000-as-arbitrum-surges-30-on-robinhood-chain-revenue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bitcoin consolidates near $78,000 as Arbitrum surges 30% on Robinhood Chain revenue</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Issuer strategies are splitting into two models:</strong> <em>Institutional cash rail</em> programs (low holder counts, large AUM per holder\u2014e.g. BUIDL, USYC, iBENJI, USTB) vs <em>global yield / distribution</em> products (broader holder bases, retail- or UCITS-friendly framing\u2014e.g. USDY, WTGXX, BENJI, USTBL). These behave like different businesses under the same \"tokenized MMF\" label. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/thailand-sec-retail-overseas-crypto-derivatives?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thailand SEC proposes retail access to regulated overseas crypto derivatives</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
